extraction_notes: |
  - Printed 52-53 (renders p053-p054), inside the Quillback entry: the paragraph opens at the foot of printed 52 and the skill rule is on printed 53.
  - The whole definition is one sentence on printed 53: in skills the Scavenger is identical to the Vagabond Optional O.C.C., except that it has detect ambush and detect concealment and traps as O.C.C. skills, does not have animal husbandry as an O.C.C. skill, and selects eight O.C.C. related skills to start with, Vagabond restrictions still applying. The skills block is therefore the stored vagabond-peasant block (Palladium Fantasy RPG Main Book p.99) with those three changes: two skills added, Animal Husbandry removed, related count 8 where the Vagabond has 6. The Hand to Hand price, the related categories and their bonuses, the later related picks and the secondary skills are the Vagabond''s, unchanged.
  - Detect Ambush and "detect concealment and traps" are printed with no percentage, so each is stored at the catalog base (30 and 25). The catalog row for the second is Detect Concealment.
  - EXPERIENCE: the book contradicts itself. Printed 53 says the Scavenger has "the same experience point requirements as a Thief or a Merchant O.C.C."; printed 215 prints a "Quillback Scavenger R.C.C." column of its own. Stored: the printed-215 column, lower bounds 0, 1901, 3601, 7201, 14401, 24501, 35001, 45001, 65001, 85001, 115001, 145001, 185001, 250001, 310001 (level 15 ends at 375,000). The Thief and Merchant ladder in the Main Book is a different one (1851, 3701, 7401, 13001 ...), so the two statements cannot both hold.
  - occ_group is optional: the class is defined by the Vagabond, which the Main Book files under Optional O.C.C.s. For the same reason men_of_arms is false; the entry prints no S.D.C. of its own, and the Quillback''s racial 15 comes from the race.
  - The entry prints no attribute requirements, no O.C.C. bonuses, no starting money and no equipment line, and says the Scavenger matches the Vagabond "in skills" only. None is stated here: no starting_money and no equipment_starting. The Vagabond''s kit includes clothing and hard leather armor, which a Quillback cannot wear (printed 53).
  - Alignment is a note in the book ("almost never be of a good alignment. Selfish alignments are most common"), which is a tendency rather than a limit; it is a restrictions line and the evil tag is not used.
  - race_restrictions names quillback, the race this R.C.C. is printed under. Printed 215 says 20-25% of Quillbacks are Scavengers.
